-- 07: Host Objects and Capabilities
-- The Host granted this Script: `storage` (suspending), `clock` (immediate),
-- `http` (suspending), `log` (immediate). Nothing else is reachable.

on remember key, value
  ask storage to save key, value and wait
  -- ALT: storage.save(key, value)                 -- [advanced]? method call style
  -- ALT: call save of storage with key, value
  -- ALT: tell storage to save key, value
  -- ?? What does a Capability look like at the call site? Options:
  --    1. Host-defined commands: the Host registers a command grammar (`save … as … in storage`).
  --       Most English, but Hosts extend the syntax. Big grammar question.
  --    2. Uniform call: `storage.save(key, value)` or `save(storage, key, value)`.
  --    3. Uniform verb: `tell storage to save key, value` / `ask storage for key`.
  --       No syntax extension; `ask` = suspending with a result in `it`.
end remember

on recall key
  ask storage to load key and wait     -- suspends: `and wait` (ADR 0019)
  if it is nothing then return "unknown"
  return it
end recall

on fetchPage url
  ask http to get url and wait
  -- ALT: put the body of (ask http to get url) into html
  put the body of it into html
  if the status of it is not 200 then tell log to write "bad status " & the status of it
  -- ?? Calling a revoked Capability is an ordinary error (sandbox contract).
  --    Its shape is error-handling fog.
end fetchPage

on stamp
  ask clock to now                   -- immediate: no `and wait`, not a Suspension Point
  put it into t
  -- ?? Nothing in the source says whether a call suspends. ADR 0004 says Hosts
  --    declare it, so the loader knows. Should the syntax show it? `ask` for
  --    suspending, `get`/`put … from` for immediate would make it visible.
end stamp

-- Host Objects have identity; copying the handle copies the handle only.
on openDoor d
  put d into same
  set the state of same to "open"
  -- ALT: put "open" into the state of same
  -- ?? For Script maps, `put … into the x of m` rebinds m (Value Semantics).
  --    For a Host Object, `the state of d` is a Host property, and the write goes
  --    to the Host. Same syntax, very different effect. `set` for Host
  --    properties only would make the difference visible (HyperTalk had `set`).
  if same = d then say "same door"       -- identity
  send opened to the room of d
end openDoor
